# EDB Documentation 

> Comprehensive documentation for EDB (EnterpriseDB) products, Postgres tools, and cloud-native database solutions.

> Full site: https://www.enterprisedb.com/docs/

The Markdown for any page under https://www.enterprisedb.com/docs/ can be retrieved by sending the request with an `Accept: text/markdown` header, or by adding ".md" to the page's URL: https://www.enterprisedb.com/docs/pgd/latest/planning.md (".mdx", and "index.md" for a section's index page, work too).

Each Markdown page begins with a YAML frontmatter block:

- title: the page's title
- description: a short summary of the page, when it has one
- product: the name of the product or section the page belongs to
- version: the product version the page documents, on every page of a versioned product (the precise version where the docs give one, else the version in the page's URL)
- url: the page's URL on the site
- lastModified: when the page's source last changed (ISO 8601)

Next come the page's title, as a heading, and its content, with every link absolute. An index page ends with links to the topics in its section, each with its description.

